Cantus Taeyang Becca says that in the  past French automaker said when produced  legendary models like the de s and the  douche evolve  but recently unusual and innovative cars  like these have been missing from its  model range the c4 cactus seems to  change that it's novel approach sets it  apart from its competitors is this the  next French Revolution John says it's  when calls these air-filled side panels  air bumps they protect the paint job  from getting scratched or dented while  parking or out shopping saving you money  on pricey touch-up jobs and repairs Yan  says saving is one of the c4 cactuses  major concepts on weight as well as  money  the base model cactus has a curb weight  of just one thousand forty kilos two  hundred less than the Citroen c4 compact  to shed weight the car makers engineers  trimmed down the platform and did  without some extra equipment the c4  cactus has a starting price of just  under fourteen thousand euros though our  test car with a 60 kilowatt engine sells  for around sixteen thousand five hundred  the cactuses rounded front features  modern LED daytime running lights above  the halogen headlights dirty air bumps  on the sides and two at the front and  back provide protection from dings and  scratches cetanas also replaced  traditional winddown rear windows with  pop-out ones that alone makes the car 11  kilos lighter the rear seat bench only  folds down in one piece which sits when  claimed saves another 6 kilos God says  that for its relatively small price you  can't expect real leather upholstery but  he feels sin has managed to give the  cactuses interior a high-quality feel  mainly through the use of different  surface materials he says everything's  very minimalist and focused on what's  important he especially likes the  luggage strap door handles together with  the aluminum door openers Andy approves  of the glove compartment design which  resembles suitcases of the 1960s and 70s  to make space for that large and [ __ ]  glove compartment the front passenger  air bag has been moved and is now  elegantly stowed in the roof  Yan says the two modern displays at the  front contrasts nicely with the retro  luggage look though the first display  only tells him his speed and how much  gas he has in the tank  there's no tachometer for instance but  he can't control all of the other  functions over the touchscreen like the  sat-nav or the climate control yan says  it all works really well though he'd  like the system to react a bit quicker  as he has to control almost every  function by a touchscreen Citroen has  found ways of saving on cost weight and  resources on even the most banal  equipment like the windshield washer  system called magic wash its washer Jets  are fitted in the tips of the wipers to  provide a bead of liquid rather than a  spray so there's no loss of visibility  when washing the system saves on window  washer fluid too so the fluid reservoir  can be smaller and therefore lighter  from fine but how does the c4 cactus  Drive John finds the steering very  smooth and the suspension quite soft so  you barely notice when you go over bumpy  roads though the suspension is a bit too  soft for his taste and like the do  cheveux before it he says the cactus  tends to shudder a bit when starting and  braking so maybe it's not the automotive  revolution we've been waiting for that's  undergone fields what's really special  about the c4 cactus is that citron has  built a back-to-basics car it has few  bells and whistles but doesn't scrimp on  comfort either it's packaged in a fresh  design at an affordable price so the  cactus c4 could be called a mini  revolution after all
 

